1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"phase-3--3d-understand-native-conversation","kind":"phase-article","route":"/roadmap/phase-3/3d-understand-native-conversation","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/phase-3/3d-understand-native-conversation","sourceHash":"93389d2289aa82860a23016029aae0258e6f84f16742ede8f03a5eb60a1ea1ed","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:51.209Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"3D — Understand Native Conversation","zh":"3D — 理解母语者对话"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"what-youre-doing","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What You're Doing","zh":"你正在做什么"}},{"id":"segment-0002","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Your listening is strong — you can follow TV, podcasts, and videos without subtitles. Now it's time to make sure you can understand real people in real conversations, and to start preparing for speaking.","zh":"你的听力已经很强——无需字幕也能听懂电视节目、播客和视频。现在是时候确保自己能够理解真实对话中的真实人物，并开始为说话做准备了。"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Conversation is different from media. People talk faster, use more filler words, interrupt each other, trail off mid-sentence, and use slang and expressions that rarely appear in scripted content.","zh":"对话与媒体内容不同。人们说话更快，会使用更多填充词，彼此打断，说到一半停住，还会使用脚本内容中很少出现的俚语和表达。"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"On the other hand, conversation is often <em>easier</em> in some ways: the topics are simpler, you can see the person's face and gestures, and you can ask them to repeat something.","zh":"另一方面，对话在某些方面往往<em>更容易</em>：话题更简单，你能看到对方的表情和手势，还可以请对方重复。"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This sub-phase also introduces your first real speaking-adjacent activities, namely crosstalk. You won't be speaking much in the target language yet, but you'll be practicing the comprehension side of a conversation with a real person.","zh":"这一子阶段还会引入你第一次真正接近口语的活动，即跨语对话。你暂时不会大量使用目标语言说话，但会和真实的人练习对话中的理解能力。"}},{"id":"whats-new","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What's New","zh":"有什么新内容"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Crosstalk</strong> — A conversation where each person speaks their native language. You speak your native language; your partner speaks the target language. This lets you focus entirely on understanding what they're saying, without the added stress of having to produce the language yourself. It's an incredibly effective way to train conversational listening because you're engaging with a real person who speaks at a natural pace, directly to you. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/crosstalk\">Crosstalk</a>","zh":"<strong>跨语对话</strong>——每个人都使用自己的母语进行交流的对话。你说自己的母语，对方说目标语言。这样你可以全神贯注地理解对方所说的内容，不必额外承受自己组织语言的压力。这是训练对话听力极其有效的方式，因为你是在直接与真实的人互动，对方以自然的速度对你说话。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/crosstalk\">跨语对话</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Conversational content</strong> — Shift your freeflow listening toward more conversational material: casual vlogs, podcasts with multiple speakers, unscripted YouTube content, interview shows. This exposes you to the rhythms and patterns of natural conversation. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/casual-vs-scripted-vs-careful-speech\">Casual vs Scripted vs Careful Speech</a>","zh":"<strong>对话类内容</strong>——将自由流听力转向更多对话类材料：轻松随意的 vlog、多位说话者参与的播客、未经脚本设计的 YouTube 内容和访谈节目。这会让你接触自然对话的节奏和模式。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/casual-vs-scripted-vs-careful-speech\">随意、脚本化与谨慎的言语</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Pronunciation practice</strong> — As a secondary activity, start working on your ability to produce the sounds of the language. You're not speaking (putting your thoughts into language), but beginning to prepare your mouth and brain for output. Chorusing is an excellent way to start this. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/chorusing\">Chorusing</a> <a href=\"/roadmap/library/learning-pronunciation\">Learning Pronunciation</a>","zh":"<strong>发音练习</strong>——作为次要活动，开始练习发出该语言声音的能力。你还不是在说话（把想法转换成语言），但正在为输出准备口腔和大脑。跟读是开始这一练习的绝佳方式。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/chorusing\">跟读</a><a href=\"/roadmap/library/learning-pronunciation\">学习发音</a>"}},{"id":"your-routine","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Your Routine","zh":"你的日常安排"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Freeflow becomes your biggest time block, with crosstalk sessions several times a week: <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">The Pillars of Language Learning</a>","zh":"自由流听力成为你占用时间最多的部分，每周进行数次跨语对话：<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning\">语言学习的支柱</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<strong>Priming:</strong> 10%","zh":"<strong>预热：</strong>10%"},{"en":"<strong>Interactive Immersion:</strong> 40%","zh":"<strong>互动沉浸：</strong>40%"},{"en":"<strong>Freeflow Immersion:</strong> 50%","zh":"<strong>自由流沉浸：</strong>50%"}]},{"id":"sample-daily-schedule","type":"heading","level":3,"content":{"en":"Sample Daily Schedule","zh":"每日安排示例"}},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Vocab study: 10 mins","zh":"词汇学习：10分钟"},{"en":"Sentence Mining while Listening: 40 mins","zh":"听力中的句子挖掘：40分钟"},{"en":"Crosstalk conversation (3x per week): 30 mins","zh":"跨语对话（每周3次）：30分钟"},{"en":"Conversational podcast/freeflow listening (on non-crosstalk days): 30 mins","zh":"对话类播客/自由流听力（非跨语对话日）：30分钟"},{"en":"Freeflow Listening: 20 mins","zh":"自由流听力：20分钟"},{"en":"Freeflow Reading: 20 mins","zh":"自由流阅读：20分钟"}]},{"id":"when-to-move-on","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Move On","zh":"何时进入下一阶段"}},{"id":"segment-0016","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Move to Phase 4 when you:","zh":"满足以下条件后进入第4阶段："}},{"id":"segment-0017","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Can have a 30-minute crosstalk conversation and only need to ask about 3 or fewer unfamiliar words, and only need your partner to repeat or rephrase fewer than 3 times","zh":"能够进行30分钟的跨语对话，只需询问3个或更少的不熟悉词语，并且只需让对方重复或换一种说法少于3次"},{"en":"Feel confident that you can understand a native speaker in casual conversation","zh":"相信自己能够听懂母语者在轻松随意对话中的表达"}]}],"cards":[]}}]
